---
import CaseStudyLayout from '../layouts/CaseStudyLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';

const email = site.email || 'janeh0120@gmail.com';
---

<CaseStudyLayout
  title="Migration Dashboard"
  heading="Complex migrations shouldn't require experts."
  role="Product Designer"
  team="1 Product Manager, 3 Developers"
  timeline="March 2026-Present"
  projectType="Product Design"
  commentId="case-study-migration"
>
  <section id="outline" data-comment-id="migration-outline" class="migration-outline">
    <p class="lead">
      I joined an early-stage, startup-like beta as the sole designer—defining design direction and
      what success looked like.
    </p>
    <p>
      The product is a complex internal tool for engineers and technical program managers making
      code updates across teams like QuickBooks—updating dependencies, swapping hardcoded values
      for tokens, and more. Agents discover needed fixes and apply the changes so teams spend less
      time on manual work.
    </p>
    <p>
      I navigated vibe-coded early designs, reverse-engineered the product, learned a technical
      space quickly, and thought strategically about where it should go next.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section data-comment-id="migration-nda">
    <aside class="migration-disclaimer" role="note" aria-label="NDA notice">
      <p>
        I’m not able to publicize this work due to an NDA. If you’d like to learn more, please
        <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>contact me personally</a> for details.
      </p>
    </aside>
  </section>
</CaseStudyLayout>

<style>
  .migration-disclaimer {
    padding: 1rem 0;
    background: transparent;
  }

  .migration-disclaimer p {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--color-muted);
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
    font-weight: 400;
    letter-spacing: 0;
  }

  .migration-disclaimer a {
    color: var(--color-ink);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 0.15em;
    transition: opacity 0.15s ease;
  }

  .migration-disclaimer a:hover {
    opacity: 0.7;
  }

  .migration-outline p + p {
    margin-top: 1em;
  }
</style>
